GitHub Actions Pipeline Issue I Faced (Docker Deployment)

While working on a project using GitHub Actions to build and deploy a Docker container, I faced a confusing issue.

❌ Problem
The GitHub Actions workflow succeeded, Docker image was built and pushed successfully.
But after deployment, the application was still running old code.

Pipeline logs showed everything green ✅
But the UI didn’t reflect the latest changes.

🔍 Root Cause
I was using the same Docker image tag (latest) for every build.
During deployment, Docker reused the existing image, instead of pulling the new one.

So technically:
Pipeline ✔️
Deployment ✔️
Application ❌ (still old version)

🛠️ Fix
I changed the pipeline to:
Use unique image tags (GitHub commit SHA / run number)
Pull the updated image during deployment
After that, every deployment reflected the latest changes correctly.

🧠 Lesson Learned
A successful pipeline doesn’t always mean a successful deployment.
Versioning Docker images properly is mandatory in CI/CD.
